  01_01 Basic & Setup

-- Installing MYSQL Server & Workbench


1. Download MySQL Installer

Go to the official page:
MySQL Community Server Download

Choose:
https://dev.mysql.com/downloads/mysql/?utm_source=chatgpt.com

MySQL Installer for Windows (x86, 64-bit)
2. Run the installer

Open the downloaded .msi file.

You will see setup options:

Developer Default (recommended)
MySQL Server
MySQL Workbench (GUI)
MySQL Shell

OR

Server Only (only database server)

3. Configure MySQL Server

During setup:

Type: Standalone MySQL Server
Port: 3306 (default)
Authentication: Use Strong Password Encryption

Set:

Username: root
Password: choose a strong password

Save your password — you will need it later.

4. Start MySQL service

The installer will automatically:

Create Windows service: MySQL80
Set it to start automatically on boot

5. Test installation

Open Command Prompt (CMD):

mysql -u root -p

Enter your password.

If you enter MySQL shell → installation is successful ✔

MySQL Workbench (GUI tool)

If you installed Developer Default:

Open MySQL Workbench and create a connection:

Host: localhost
Port: 3306
Username: root
Password: your password
 Linux (Ubuntu / Debian)
sudo apt update
sudo apt install mysql-server -y

Start MySQL:

sudo systemctl start mysql
sudo systemctl enable mysql

Secure installation:

sudo mysql_secure_installation
 macOS (Homebrew)
brew install mysql
brew services start mysql
 Verify installation

Check version:

mysql --version

Or inside MySQL:

SELECT VERSION();
